INT. FAMILY MINIVAN - PARKED AT A DRIVE-IN - NIGHT

Back seat. The movie flickers through the windshield. Popcorn spills.

NADINE OKORO-LANCASTER, 16, sits in the back with her little brother, RUFUS, 9, who holds a box of candy. In the front, their mother, GRETCHEN LANCASTER-PRICE, 40s, glances at the rear-view mirror. A phone buzzes in the cupholder.

NADINE
Rufus, quit kicking the seat.

RUFUS
I'm not.

GRETCHEN
You are, honey.

RUFUS
It's the movie.

NADINE
The movie doesn't kick.

Gretchen picks up the phone. Reads the screen. Her face stiffens. She answers on speaker.

COACH TANAKA (V.O.)
(over phone)
Mrs. Lancaster-Price? It's about Nadine. She missed practice again.

Nadine freezes. Rufus stops chewing.

GRETCHEN
(evenly)
Thank you, Coach. We'll talk.

COACH TANAKA (V.O.)
(over phone)
I just want her to know there's a spot.

GRETCHEN
Thank you.

She hangs up. A long silence. On the screen, an actress screams. Nadine stares at her knees.

GRETCHEN (CONT'D)
Nadine.

NADINE
I can explain.

GRETCHEN
Please do.

NADINE
I don't want to play.

RUFUS ^
She's been going to the library instead.

NADINE
Rufus!

RUFUS
Sorry!

Gretchen watches them in the mirror. Then she reaches back and puts a hand on Nadine's knee. It stays there. On screen, the credits roll.
